It seems there is a persistent issue with the interface. Let's proceed with the calculation manually and provide the final answer.

The formula to calculate the percentage is:
\[ \text{Percentage} = \left( \frac{\text{December 2012 shares}}{\text{Fourth quarter shares}} \right) \times 100 \]

Using the values from the table:
- Total number of shares purchased in December 2012: 102400
- Total number of shares purchased in the fourth quarter: 619314

So the calculation is:
\[ \text{Percentage} = \left( \frac{102400}{619314} \right) \times 100 \]

Performing the calculation:
\[ \text{Percentage} = \left( 0.1651 \right) \times 100 \approx 16.51\% \]

The final answer is:
\[ \boxed{16.51\%} \]

This is the percentage of the total number of shares purchased in December 2012 out of the total fourth quarter shares.